{"id":"word:hebrew:H1101","type":"word","title":"בָּלַל","subtitle":"H1101 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to overflow (specifically with oil.); by implication, to mix ; to fodder","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to בָּלַל (H1101) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 43 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"בָּלַל (bâlal) means to overflow (specifically with oil.); by implication, to mix ; to fodder First listed occurrence: Exod 29 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"בָּלַל","transliteration":"bâlal","pronunciation":"baw-lal'","strong":"H1101","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1101","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["בְּלוּלָ֥ה","בְּלוּלָ֣ה","בְּלוּלֹ֣ת","בָּל֥וּל","בָּל֨וּל"],"morphs":[["HVqsfsa",29],["HVqsfpa",5],["HVqsmsa",4],["HC/Vqh1cp",1],["HVqp3ms",1],["HVri3ms",1],["HC/Vqw3ms",1],["HVqp1cs",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"to overflow (specifically with oil.); by implication, to mix ; to fodder","usage":"anoint, confound, × fade, mingle, mix (self), give provender, temper.","full":"H1101. balal I. בָּלַל verb mingle, mix, confuse, confound (Arabic moisten (with water), compare moisture , Assyrian balâlu , Dl Pr 70 ; compare Phoenician בלל name of a sacrifice, & Late Hebrew בִּלְבֵּל ; Aramaic בַּלְבֵּל , ) — Qal Perfect בָּלַל Gen 11:9 , ַבּלֹּתִָּֽי Psa 92:11 (but compare below); Imperfect 1plural נָָֽבְלָה = נָכֹ֫לָּה Gen 11:7 , compare Kö i. 325 ; Participle passive בָּלוּל Exod 29:40 3 t., בְּלוּלָה Lev 2:5 28t., בְּלוּלֹת Exod 29:2 4 t.; — 1 mingle, confuse (object שָׂפָה = speech, language, q. v.) Gen 11:7 , 9 (J). 2 mix (cakes or flour, etc. always with oil) technical term of sacrifice, only P (H Lev 23:13 ), compare Di on 2:4 ; usually as בּ ׳סֹלֶת ׳בַּשֶּׁמֶן מנחה, Exod 29:40 ; Lev 2:5 ; 14:10 , 21 ; 23:13 ; Num 7:13 , 19 , 25 , 31 , 37 , 43 , 49 , 55 , 61 , 67 , 73, 79; 8:8 ; 15:4 , 6 , 9 ; 28:5 , 9 , 12 (twice in verse); 28:13 ; 28:20 ; 28:28 ; 29:3 ; 23:9 ; 23:14 , ב ׳מנחה ׳בשׁ Lev 7:10 (opposed to חֲרֵבָה ) 9:4 , ב מַצּוֺת ׳חַלּוֺת ׳בשׁ Exod 29:2 ; Lev 7:12 (twice in verse), i.e. made by mixing with oil; ב מצות ׳חלות ׳בשׁ סלת 2:4 , ב חלות ׳סלת ׳בשׁ Num 6:15 , i.e. fine flour (in the form) of cakes so made. רַעֲנָן בְּשֶׁמֶן ַבּלֹּתִָּֽי Psa 92:11 I shall be ( am ) anointed with fresh oil AV RV; verb not elsewhere in this sense; ᵑ9 ᵐ5 Hup Che read בְּלֹתִי from בלה , infinitive construct suffix, abstract for concrete, my wasting = my wasting strength , of declining age; Israel under figure of old man; this however is not favoured by context. The passage is therefore doubtful. Hithpo`el Imperfect יִתְבּוֺלָ֑ל Hosea 7:8 ; י הוא בעמים ׳אפרים Ephraim, among the peoples doth he mix himself ; but Ew Now derive here from בלל = בלה (or נבל ) waste away , compare Hiph`il Hiph`il Imperfect וַנָּ֫בֶל Isa 64:5 and we faded away , but read perhaps וַנִּכֹּל from נבל compare Di (De, less probably, derives from בלל — compare Ew Now Hosea 7:8 — or בול = נבל ). II. [ בָּלַל ] verb denominative to give provender — Qal Imperfect וַיָּ֑בָל Judg 19:21 Qr (Kt ויבול ) followed by לְ give provender to the asses.","rootNote":"a primitive root; (also denominatively from 1098 ) to fodder","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"Exod 29 2","keyReferences":["Exod 29 2","Exod 29 40","Gen 11 7","Gen 11 9","Hos 7 8","Judg 19 21","Lev 2 4","Lev 2 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":43,"occurrences":[{"reference":"Exod 29 2","book":"Exod","chapter":29,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בְּלוּלֹ֣ת","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsfpa"},{"reference":"Exod 29 40","book":"Exod","chapter":29,"verse":40,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּל֨וּל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqsmsa"},{"reference":"Gen 11 7","book":"Gen","chapter":11,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/נָבְלָ֥ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC